<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Salamis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/480-bce">480 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-persian-wars">Greco-Persian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Salamis was a naval battle fought in 480 BCE in the straits between the island of Salamis and the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a>, during the second Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-persian-invasion-of-greece">invasion of Greece</a>. The allied Greek fleet, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/themistocles">Themistocles</a>, defeated the larger fleet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xerxes-i">Xerxes I</a>, who then withdrew with much of his army to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. The victory prepared the way for the Greek success at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-plataea">Plataea</a> the next year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-salamis.jpg" alt="Battle of Salamis" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Department of History, United States Military Academy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_salamis.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
